# deploy/backup.env.example
#
# Template for /srv/framecast/env/backup.env — loaded by
# framecast-backup.service via EnvironmentFile=. Copy this file to the
# server, fill in every placeholder, then chmod 600 it. The real file lives
# ONLY at /srv/framecast/env/backup.env on the VPS and is never committed —
# see docs/vps-deployment.md, backup and restore section.
#
# This file (the .example one) intentionally contains no secrets: every
# value below is either a placeholder in <angle brackets> naming where the
# real value comes from, or a fixed setting that's safe to commit as-is.

# From the Cloudflare dashboard: R2 > Manage API tokens for the access key
# pair, and the bucket's own settings page for the endpoint and name.
# R2_ENDPOINT is account-specific: https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_BUCKET=<r2-bucket-name>
R2_ENDPOINT=<https://ACCOUNT_ID.r2.cloudflarestorage.com>
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<r2-access-key-id>
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<r2-secret-access-key>

# R2 ignores the actual region value, but the AWS CLI refuses to run with
# none configured at all. "auto" is Cloudflare's own documented placeholder;
# backup.sh also defaults to it if this line is left out entirely.
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=auto

# Must match POSTGRES_USER in /srv/framecast/.env — the file Compose itself
# reads for interpolation (see deploy/README.md) — not prod.env/staging.env.
POSTGRES_USER=<postgres-user>

# Optional. A healthchecks.io (or compatible) ping URL for this job, e.g.
# https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>. If set, backup.sh pings "<url>/start" when it
# begins, "<url>" (bare) once both databases have uploaded successfully, and
# "<url>/fail" on any failure. Point a healthchecks.io check with a grace
# period past 03:00 UTC at this URL and a night where the timer never fires
# at all — box down, timer disabled, a systemd typo — is caught by the
# monitoring service's own missed-check-in alert, not just failures that
# happen to run and then error out loudly. Leave unset to skip monitoring
# entirely; backup.sh runs exactly the same either way, just unobserved.
#
# Left EMPTY, not filled with a placeholder, on purpose. backup.sh only skips
# monitoring when this is empty or unset; any non-empty value counts as
# configured, so an unedited file would curl a literal placeholder URL every
# night, swallow the failure (`|| true` — a monitoring hiccup must never fail
# the backup), and leave the operator believing the job is watched when no
# ping has ever arrived. Empty fails honestly: no monitoring, and nothing
# claiming otherwise. Set it to a real https://hc-ping.com/<uuid> to enable.
HEALTHCHECK_PING_URL=
